{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:57:17.102Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"read_files","toolCallId":"toolu_01XbuipZvFtPugWEAG3kv1D2","output":[{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\.cline-runs\\run-152706-g9km.task.md","result":"1 | # Instructions for Cline run run-152706-g9km (mode: act, model: Cline default, started 2026-10-10T09:57:06.109Z)\n2 | \n3 | Read .clinerules and memory-bank, then do tasks/NEXT.md (T3). Finish by running test, typecheck, lint and build, updating tasks/LOG.md, and committing.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\NEXT.md","result":" 1 | # NEXT TASK: T3, Cline SDK Rule Maintenance Agent (the bonus criterion)\n 2 | \n 3 | T2 reviewed: 150/150 tests and the build pass. Answers to your requests:\n 4 | - Leaving out `export const runtime` (because of cacheComponents): **approved**. Keep the comment in each route.\n 5 | - \"Type it in\": a document counts as added **only once its name field (or the main field for that doc type) has a value**.\n 6 |   Fix this first (small) with a test.\n 7 | \n 8 | Then do `tasks/backlog/T3-cline-agent.md` (PLAN briefly at the top of your log entry, then ACT). Notes:\n 9 | - `.env.local` now has `CLINE_API_KEY` and `CLINE_MODEL`. Install `@cline/sdk` (Node 22+ is available). If its API differs from .clinerules/03-stack.md, read the package's own README/types in node_modules and follow them; record what you found in `memory-bank/techContext.md`.\n10 | - The agent must work through **tools only** (`getRuleSchema`, `getCurrentRule`, `proposeRule`, `runTests`, `saveProposal`): it proposes data validated by zod, never writes source files.\n11 | - Keep tests offline: mock the agent; unit-test the tools and store directly.\n12 | - Admin page `/admin`: paste box with two \"Load demo notice\" buttons (the two files in docs/), a live tool-call log, a readable before/after diff, test results (new + regression), and Publish / Reject. Version history per scheme. Published versions take effect in the citizen flow immediately.\n13 | - If `node:sqlite` causes build trouble, a JSON file store under `data/` (gitignored) is acceptable, with the same one-writer rule.\n14 | - Put a manual live check in `scripts/agent-smoke.mjs` that runs both demo notices against the real API and prints the results.\n15 | \n16 | **Done when:** T3's \"Done when\" holds (both demo notices produce passing, publishable proposals; existing regression tests still pass), all checks pass, LOG.md updated, committed \"T3: Cline SDK rule maintenance agent\".","success":true}],"durationMs":16}}
