{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:57:22.323Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"read_files","toolCallId":"toolu_01DMYeeTD6FSD1KiEULseMh2","output":[{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\activeContext.md","result":" 1 | # Active context\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Current state\n 4 | T2 (main flow) is done. One mobile flow on `/` (client component `src/app/_components/KaagazApp.tsx`): scheme cards (PM-KISAN first, \"flagship\") → documents (photo per slot via `/api/extract`, \"type it in\", or samples A/B/C with a purple \"Demo mode: fake sample documents\" label) → confirm fields (low confidence in amber) → big Yes/No questions → report from `/api/check`. The report shows the Eligibility banner, the Readiness banner (+ \"check at the bank\" list), Fix before you apply, Please verify, OK (collapsed), benefit (central / state top-up separately), supporting docs, a print-only cover sheet and the bilingual disclaimer. Assamese default, English toggle (`src/i18n.ts`).\n 5 | 150 tests pass; typecheck, lint and build are clean. The live Cline API reads a fake Aadhaar image correctly (image input works).\n 6 | \n 7 | ## Decisions made in T2\n 8 | - `src/server/ai.ts` is the only model caller: `extractDocument(image, hint?, deps?)` → `{ doc, detectedDocType } | { error: ai_unavailable | ai_failed | invalid_image }`, one retry, logs only model/promptVersion/inputHash/outcome. The Cline API wraps responses as `{ data: { choices } }`; both shapes are handled.\n 9 | - Raw model JSON → `ExtractedDoc` in pure `src/core/extraction.ts` (full Aadhaar → last 4; unscored AI fields → 0.5 confidence so they get confirmed; non-ISO DOB → low confidence).\n10 | - Route files do NOT export `runtime = \"nodejs\"`: Next 16.4 rejects it with `cacheComponents` (Node is the default anyway). Awaiting Claude's confirmation.\n11 | - Nothing is read from the death certificate or BPL proof (presence only); `husbandName` is not collected.\n12 | - The client never imports the engine: UI helpers live in `flow.ts`, `reportView.ts`, `catalog.ts`, `thresholds.ts`; the page (a server component) passes a plain `SchemeView[]` catalog.\n13 | - \"Type it in\" adds an empty document (counted as present by the engine); flagged for Claude.\n14 | \n15 | ## Decisions made in T1\n16 | - Brief v2: **Assamese default + English**; two verdicts (eligibility, readiness); provenance on every rule (verified vs provisional).\n17 | - `RuleProvenance.sourceUrl` is nullable, but a `verified` rule must have one (schema refine). Provisional overrides from the T3 agent can start with `sourceUrl: null`.\n18 | - `ExtractedDoc.fields` is strict and only holds `aadhaarLast4` (never a full Aadhaar number). A missing per-field confidence means \"entered/confirmed by the user\"; < 0.8 → needs_verification.\n19 | - The name reference document is Aadhaar for PM-KISAN and the widow pension, and the ration card for Orunodoi.\n20 | - A PM-KISAN land-owner mismatch becomes `needs_verification` (not ok) if the user answers `land_in_family_member_name` = yes (farmer family = spouse/minor children).\n21 | - Orunodoi question ids: `nfsa_enrolled` (requirement); any-of `widow | person_with_disability | aay_card | income_below_2_lakh`; exclusions `elected_representative | professional | govt_staff_or_pensioner | contractor_or_trader | large_landholder | four_wheeler | similar_state_scheme`. All provisional.\n22 | - Widow pension: all mandatory docs (incl. `bpl_proof`) are provisional (\"commonly required; confirm locally\"); age and BPL are verified.\n23 | - The registry is in-memory: `registerScheme` validates, rejects a duplicate id+version and keeps old versions. T3 will persist versions in SQLite and register them at startup.\n24 | - Assamese strings in `labels.ts`, the scheme packs and `rejectionCodes.ts` are drafts awaiting native-speaker review (Das).\n25 | \n26 | ## Next step\n27 | T3: Rule Maintenance Agent (`@cline/sdk`, `node:sqlite` `rule_versions`, regression tests + human approval, versioned packs). Before the demo: a phone click-through of the T2 flow and native-speaker review of `src/i18n.ts`.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\productContext.md","result":" 1 | # Product context: KaagazCheck (কাগজ চেক): \"Check before you apply\"\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Why it exists\n 4 | Eligible people lose welfare benefits *after* applying: names that don't match across Aadhaar, bank and land records; Aadhaar not seeded to the bank; missing certificates; rejection reasons they cannot understand. Documented example: Rajasthan 2019, only about 23% of registered PM-KISAN farmers got the 3rd instalment, mostly because of Aadhaar name mismatches (sources in `docs/research.md`).\n 5 | \n 6 | KaagazCheck checks the papers **before** the person applies, in **Assamese (default) with an English toggle**, and says exactly what to fix and where.\n 7 | **Promise:** we help catch preventable mistakes. We do NOT guarantee approval; the department decides.\n 8 | \n 9 | ## Users\n10 | - **Citizen** in Assam (farmer, widow, woman of a household) on a basic Android phone, often helped by family or a CSC/NGO helper.\n11 | - **Rule maintainer** (helper organisation) who keeps scheme rules current with the Rule Maintenance Agent (Cline SDK).\n12 | \n13 | ## Schemes in scope (rule packs v2, `docs/schemes.md` is the source of truth)\n14 | - **PM-KISAN** (`pm-kisan`): flagship end-to-end demo. No landholding-size limit.\n15 | - **Orunodoi 3.0, Assam** (`orunodoi-3`): only the ration card and ₹1,250/month are verified; everything else is provisional → \"needs verification\".\n16 | - **Widow Pension IGNWPS** (`nsap-widow`): age 40–79, BPL, central ₹300/month; state top-up unconfirmed.\n17 | \n18 | ## Main demo path (3 minutes)\n19 | 1. Pick a scheme.\n20 | 2. Add documents: photo, or \"Use sample A/B/C\" (A clean PM-KISAN, B name mismatch, C widow missing death certificate).\n21 | 3. AI reads each document → fields + confidence; low confidence → the user confirms or edits.\n22 | 4. Answer the yes/no questions.\n23 | 5. Rule engine → **two verdicts**: *Eligibility* (likely_eligible / not_eligible / needs_verification) and *Readiness* (ready_for_review / action_required / needs_verification). Each check has a reason, where to fix it, and its source (provenance, verified vs provisional).\n24 | 6. Assamese report + printable cover sheet.\n25 | \n26 | ## Cline inside the product: Rule Maintenance Agent (T3)\n27 | A scheme notice → the agent proposes a rule change (new scheme or new version, with provenance) → writes regression tests → runs them through the engine → diff + test results → a **human approves** → a new rule-pack version is published (old version kept). Demo inputs: `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` (add a scheme), `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` (one-time ₹1,500 for October 2026, via a time-bounded benefit override).\n28 | \n29 | ## Second mode (T4)\n30 | Rejection decoder: rejection text → known reason code (`src/core/rejectionCodes.ts`) → fix steps in Assamese + English.\n31 | \n32 | ## Trust rules\n33 | - The AI only reads and explains; the rule engine decides.\n34 | - Every rule carries provenance; provisional rules and external facts (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified) → needs_verification, never a definitive pass/fail.\n35 | - A fuzzy name score never equals identity: only an exact (normalised) match is `ok`.\n36 | - Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images processed in memory, never stored.\n37 | - Demo uses fake sample documents only. AI-generated Assamese is labelled \"draft\"; fixed Assamese strings need native-speaker review.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\progress.md","result":" 1 | # Progress\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Done\n 4 | - [x] T0: Memory Bank, Next.js 16 scaffold (TS strict, Tailwind v4, ESLint), Vitest + fast-check + zod, npm scripts, `.gitignore`, `.env.example`, placeholder page, smoke test, first commit.\n 5 | - [x] T1: core rule engine v2. Step 0 (memory bank refreshed for brief v2; title \"KaagazCheck: কাগজ চেক\", taglines EN/AS, `<html lang=\"as\">`); zod types; 3 rule packs with provenance + versioned registry; name matcher (Devanagari + Assamese/Bengali transliteration, Jaro-Winkler); `ageOn`; `maskAadhaar`; `benefitOn` with overrides; `evaluate` with two verdicts; rejection codes EN/AS; samples A/B/C. 93 tests.\n 6 | \n 7 | - [x] T2: main flow. `src/server/ai.ts` (Cline API vision, zod, one retry, `{ error }` fallback), `/api/extract` + `/api/check`, pure helpers (`extraction`, `flow`, `reportView`, `catalog`), `src/i18n.ts` (as/en), mobile UI (scheme → docs/samples → confirm → questions → two-verdict report → print cover sheet). 150 tests.\n 8 | \n 9 | ## To do\n10 | - [ ] T3: Rule Maintenance Agent (`@cline/sdk`, `node:sqlite` `rule_versions`, tests + human approval, versioned packs)\n11 | - [ ] T4: rejection decoder + polish\n12 | - [ ] T-last: freeze, full README, demo path check\n13 | \n14 | ## Known issues\n15 | - `npm install` warns that eslint@9 is deprecated (pinned by eslint-config-next 16.4.0). Harmless.\n16 | - Assamese strings (incl. all of `src/i18n.ts`) are drafts; they need native-speaker review before the demo.\n17 | - The T2 UI has not been clicked through on a real phone yet (only HTML + API smoke tests).\n18 | - Route files omit `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"` (incompatible with `cacheComponents` in Next 16.4); awaiting Claude's confirmation.\n19 | - The transliteration table is basic (good enough for possible_match on common names; cross-script is never `same`).","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\projectbrief.md","result":" 1 | # Project brief v2: KaagazCheck (কাগজ চেক): \"Check before you apply\"\n 2 | \n 3 | **Pitch:** We help citizens catch preventable welfare-application mistakes *before* they submit their papers. Our AI reads the documents; a tested rule engine checks them; and Cline maintains the rules as official guidelines change.\n 4 | **Promise:** we reduce preventable errors. We do NOT guarantee approval; the department decides.\n 5 | \n 6 | ## Problem (evidence: docs/research.md)\n 7 | Eligible people lose benefits after applying because their documents disagree (name spellings across Aadhaar, bank and land record; account not Aadhaar-seeded; missing papers) or because rejections arrive unexplained. In Rajasthan in 2019, only about 23% of registered PM-KISAN farmers got the third instalment, mostly due to name mismatches with Aadhaar.\n 8 | \n 9 | ## Users\n10 | - **Citizen** in Assam on a basic Android phone, often helped by family or a CSC/NGO helper.\n11 | - **Rule maintainer** (helper organisation) who keeps scheme rules current using the Cline agent.\n12 | \n13 | ## Languages\n14 | **Assamese (default) + English toggle.** All fixed UI and check messages live in one `src/i18n.ts` with `as` and `en` keys. Assamese strings must be reviewed by a native speaker before the demo (Das will arrange). AI-generated Assamese (letters, explanations) is labelled \"draft\".\n15 | \n16 | ## Scope: rule packs v2 (docs/schemes.md is the source of truth)\n17 | - **PM-KISAN: flagship, full end-to-end demo** (name mismatch, missing document, uncertain bank status).\n18 | - **Orunodoi 3.0: Assam relevance, verified rules only;** provisional criteria → \"needs verification\".\n19 | - **Widow Pension (IGNWPS): simple, reliable rules** (age 40–79, BPL, central ₹300/month).\n20 | \n21 | ## Architecture (the trust design)\n22 | 1. **Document reader (AI):** extracts names, dates, account details and document type, with per-field confidence. Low confidence → user confirms.\n23 | 2. **Deterministic rule engine (pure code, tested):** normalises fields, checks consistency, evaluates verified criteria, finds missing documents. Provisional rules and external facts → `needs_verification`.\n24 | 3. **Two separate verdicts:** *Eligibility* (likely_eligible / not_eligible / needs_verification) and *Readiness* (ready_for_review / action_required / needs_verification).\n25 | 4. **Next steps:** corrections, where to go (bank, Aadhaar centre, circle office, Gram Panchayat), the source of each rule, and a printable cover sheet.\n26 | 5. **Explainer (AI, optional):** friendly wording in Assamese, built only from the engine's result.\n27 | \n28 | ## Core loop (must-ship demo path)\n29 | Pick scheme → add documents (photo, or \"Use sample A/B/C\") → confirm low-confidence fields → answer yes/no questions → two-verdict report with fixes and sources → print cover sheet.\n30 | Samples (clearly fake): A = clean PM-KISAN farmer → ready_for_review (+ bank seeding needs verification). B = PM-KISAN with \"RAMESH KR SHARMA\" (bank, possible match) and \"Rameshwar Sharma\" (land record, mismatch) → action_required. C = widow pension, missing death certificate → action_required.\n31 | \n32 | ## Cline inside the product: Rule Maintenance Agent (T3)\n33 | Upload or paste a scheme notice → a `@cline/sdk` Agent proposes a **rule change** (new scheme or edited rule, with provenance: sourceUrl, clause, effectiveDate) → writes **regression tests** → runs them through the engine (existing scheme tests must still pass) → shows a diff + test results → a **human approves** → a new rule-pack version is published (old version kept). Demo inputs: `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` (add a scheme) and `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` (a one-time payment change, to show versioning).\n34 | \n35 | ## Trust rules (non-negotiable)\n36 | - AI reads and explains; **code decides**. No eligibility claim from model text.\n37 | - Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images processed in memory, never stored.\n38 | - Every rule carries provenance; provisional → needs_verification.\n39 | - A fuzzy name score never equals identity.\n40 | - Demo uses fake documents only.\n41 | \n42 | ## Data model sketch\n43 | - `RuleProvenance` { sourceUrl, sourceTitle, clause?, effectiveDate?, verifiedOn, version, status: verified | provisional }\n44 | - `SchemeRule` { id, version, nameEn, nameAs, benefit { centralShare, stateTopUp|null, period, effectiveDate, provenance }, mandatoryDocs[], supportingDocs[], ageRange?, eligibilityAnyOf[], exclusions[], externalChecks[], each criterion with provenance }\n45 | - `ExtractedDoc` { docType, fields { name, dob, aadhaarLast4, accountNo, ifsc, ownerNames[], husbandName, ... }, confidence per field }\n46 | - `Report` { eligibility, readiness, checks[], schemeVersion, asOfDate }\n47 | - DB (T3): `rule_versions` { schemeId, version, ruleJson, testsJson, testResultJson, status: proposed | published | rejected, sourceNote, createdAt, approvedAt }\n48 | \n49 | ## Stretch\n50 | Assamese voice readout (only if the browser has an as-IN voice; otherwise hide) · rejection-notice decoder (T4) · helper mode for many applicants.\n51 | \n52 | ## Cut list (cut in this order)\n53 | Voice → decoder letter drafting → real photo upload (keep samples + manual entry) → cover-sheet styling. **Never cut:** the two-verdict report, provenance, the Cline agent with tests + approval.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\README.md","result":"1 | # Memory Bank\n2 | Empty until the problem statement is released. In task T0, Cline creates:\n3 | `projectbrief.md` (from Claude's brief), `productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `techContext.md`, `activeContext.md`, `progress.md`.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\systemPatterns.md","result":" 1 | # System patterns\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Core pipeline: AI reads → rule engine decides → AI explains\n 4 | 1. **Read (AI):** a document image or text → `ExtractedDoc` (fields + per-field confidence), validated with zod.\n 5 | 2. **Decide (pure code):** `evaluate(scheme, docs, answers, asOfDate) → Report` in `src/core/evaluate.ts`. Deterministic, unit- and property-tested. No model text ever decides a status.\n 6 | 3. **Explain (AI, optional):** friendlier Assamese wording or a letter draft, built only from the report's checks (labelled \"draft\").\n 7 | \n 8 | ## Module boundaries\n 9 | - `src/core/`: pure TypeScript. No React, network, DB, `process.env` or implicit \"today\" (`asOfDate` is always passed in).\n10 |   - `types.ts` zod schemas: `RuleProvenance`, `SchemeRule` (versioned), `ExtractedDoc`, `Answers`, `Check`, `Report`, `BenefitOn`.\n11 |   - `schemes/` rule packs (`pm-kisan.ts`, `orunodoi-3.ts`, `nsap-widow.ts`; provenance helpers in `sources.ts`) + registry `index.ts`: `getScheme(id, version?)`, `listSchemes()`, `listSchemeVersions(id)`, `registerScheme(rule)` (validates; keeps old versions; newest wins), `questionsFor(scheme)`.\n12 |   - `nameMatch.ts` (+ `transliterate.ts`), `age.ts` (`ageOn`), `aadhaar.ts` (`maskAadhaar`), `benefit.ts` (`benefitOn` with time-bounded overrides), `rejectionCodes.ts`, `labels.ts` (bilingual doc/office labels, disclaimer), `samples.ts` (fake sample sets A/B/C), `dates.ts`.\n13 |   - T2 UI helpers (pure, client-safe; they don't import the engine): `extraction.ts` (raw model JSON → `ExtractedDoc`), `docFields.ts`, `flow.ts`, `reportView.ts` (sections/tones/₹ formatting), `catalog.ts` (`SchemeView`), `thresholds.ts`.\n14 | - `src/i18n.ts` (T2): every fixed UI string in `as` + `en` (same keys, tested); reuses `labels.ts`.\n15 | - `src/server/ai.ts` (T2): the **only** module that calls a model. Structured JSON → zod → one retry → safe fallback `{ error }`. Logs model, prompt version, input hash (never raw personal data). `fetch`/`env`/`log` are injectable for tests.\n16 | - `src/server/api.ts` (T2): request schemas + handlers for `/api/check` (engine only) and `/api/extract` (via ai.ts); the route files are thin wrappers.\n17 | - `src/app/_components/` (T2): the single client flow `KaagazApp` and its steps; `page.tsx` (server) passes a plain catalog + samples.\n18 | - `src/server/store.ts` (T3): the **only** database writer (`node:sqlite`, WAL, transactions); `rule_versions` table.\n19 | - `src/server/agent/` (T3): `@cline/sdk` Rule Maintenance Agent; its tools call `src/core` (`registerScheme`, `evaluate`).\n20 | - `src/app/api/**/route.ts`: thin handlers on the Node.js runtime (the default; an explicit `runtime` export breaks the build with `cacheComponents`).\n21 | - `src/app/**`: UI (Assamese default, English toggle; fixed strings in `src/i18n.ts`). Calls API routes, never the model.\n22 | \n23 | ## Result model (docs/schemes.md v2)\n24 | - Check result: `ok | action_required | needs_verification | not_applicable`; kind: `document | name | field | eligibility | external`. Every check has `messageEn`, `messageAs`, `fixWhere`, `provenance`, plus `match` for name checks.\n25 | - **Eligibility:** `not_eligible` only when a **verified** eligibility criterion failed; any provisional, unanswered or unreadable criterion → `needs_verification`; else `likely_eligible`.\n26 | - **Readiness:** any `action_required` (missing mandatory doc, name `mismatch`, bad IFSC/account format, failed verified criterion) → `action_required`; else any non-external `needs_verification` (possible match, initials, low confidence, provisional) → `needs_verification`; else `ready_for_review`. External checks (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified, ration card active) are always `needs_verification` and listed, but on their own they don't block `ready_for_review`.\n27 | - Money: `centralShare` + `stateTopUp` (null = unconfirmed → `total` null; never show an unconfirmed total). Overrides are inclusive date windows; the last matching one wins.\n28 | \n29 | ## Name matching (showcase, defensive)\n30 | Tokenise → drop leading honorifics (SHRI/SMT/MR/MRS/KUMARI/LATE…) → transliterate Devanagari/Assamese/Bengali → canonical variants (KR→KUMAR, MD/MOHD→MOHAMMAD, DEBI→DEVI, SK→SHEIKH…). Levels: `same` (identical after formatting; the only level that gives `ok`), `possible_match` (variants, transliteration, word order, or every word pair Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85), `initials_only`, `mismatch` (incl. a missing/extra word). The score is shown but never decides.\n31 | \n32 | ## Privacy\n33 | Aadhaar: only `aadhaarLast4` is stored in `ExtractedDoc`; `maskAadhaar` → `XXXX XXXX 1234`. Images processed in memory only. Minimum personal data.\n34 | \n35 | ## Testing\n36 | Vitest + fast-check, tests first for core logic. Properties: name same-as-itself, symmetry, mask ≤ 4 digits, possible_match never `ok`, Orunodoi never `not_eligible`, evaluate deterministic + schema-valid, readiness invariant.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\techContext.md","result":" 1 | # Tech context\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Stack\n 4 | - One Next.js 16 app (App Router, `src/` dir, `@/*` → `./src/*`), React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS v4 (via `@tailwindcss/turbopack` loader in `next.config.ts`).\n 5 | - Validation: zod 4.\n 6 | - Tests: Vitest 5 (Node environment, `src/**/*.test.ts`) + fast-check 4.\n 7 | - Lint: ESLint 9 flat config (`eslint-config-next`); `next lint` no longer exists in Next 16.\n 8 | - Database (T3): built-in `node:sqlite` (WAL); fall back to `better-sqlite3` only if needed. `node:sqlite` loads on this machine.\n 9 | - AI: Cline API (OpenAI-compatible), base URL `https://api.cline.bot/api/v1`, all calls via `src/server/ai.ts`.\n10 | - In-product agent (T3): `@cline/sdk` `Agent`, `providerId: \"openai-compatible\"`, tools via `createTool` with zod schemas.\n11 | \n12 | ## Environment\n13 | - Windows, PowerShell 5.1; the path contains a space (`C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build`). Use npm scripts and cross-platform Node code.\n14 | - Node v24.21.0, npm 11.19.0, git 2.55.0.\n15 | - Secrets only in `.env.local` (git-ignored): `CLINE_API_KEY`, `CLINE_MODEL` (e.g. `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`, never a `:batch` model). The template is `.env.example`.\n16 | - Write files containing Assamese (or other non-Latin text) with the editor tool (UTF-8), not PowerShell redirection. Assamese uses ৰ (U+09F0) and ৱ (U+09F1), not Bengali র/ব.\n17 | - The editor tool rejects payloads over ~6000 characters: write large files in chunks (create, then insert at the end).\n18 | - `tsconfig.json` includes `**/*.ts`, so never leave scratch `.ts` files in the repo root while running `next build`.\n19 | \n20 | ## npm scripts\n21 | | Script | Command |\n22 | |---|---|\n23 | | `dev` | `next dev` |\n24 | | `build` | `next build` |\n25 | | `start` | `next start` |\n26 | | `lint` | `eslint .` |\n27 | | `typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |\n28 | | `test` | `vitest run` |\n29 | | `test:watch` | `vitest` |\n30 | \n31 | ## Gotchas found in T0\n32 | - Vitest 5 needs `@types/node` ≥ 22 (peer dep), so `@types/node` is `^22`.\n33 | - The Vitest config is `vitest.config.mts` (ESM); a `.ts` config triggers a Vite \"configLoader native\" warning because `package.json` has no `\"type\": \"module\"`.\n34 | - The global `LayoutProps<\"/\">` type only exists after `next build`/`next dev` generate `.next/types`, so `layout.tsx` uses an explicit `Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>` to keep `npm run typecheck` working on a clean checkout.\n35 | - Vite writes warnings to stderr, which PowerShell reports as `NativeCommandError`. Check the real exit code (e.g. run via `cmd /c ... & echo %ERRORLEVEL%`).\n36 | - `npm install` is slow here (about 5 minutes for a fresh install); long commands can exceed the tool timeout, so run them in the background with logs.\n37 | \n38 | ## Gotchas found in T2\n39 | - Next 16.4 + `cacheComponents: true` **rejects `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"`** in route files (build error). Node.js is the default runtime, so routes omit it.\n40 | - The Cline API (`/chat/completions`) returns the OpenAI body wrapped as `{ data: { choices: [...] } }`. Image input (`image_url` data URL) works with `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`.\n41 | - This PowerShell session had an **empty `CLINE_MODEL` env var** set. Next never overrides an existing env var from `.env.local`, so the AI looked unconfigured. Run `Remove-Item Env:CLINE_MODEL` before `next dev`/`next start` if `/api/extract` says `ai_unavailable` while `.env.local` is filled.\n42 | - In Vitest, `beforeEach(() => mock.mockReset())` returns the mock, which Vitest then runs as a teardown. Use a block body `beforeEach(() => { mock.mockReset(); })`.\n43 | - Manual smoke test: `npm run build`, `npx next start -p 3123`, `node scripts/smoke.mjs http://localhost:3123`.\n44 | \n45 | ## Scaffold notes\n46 | Generated with `create-next-app@16.4.0` in a temp folder and copied in (it refuses non-empty folders). Defaults kept: `cacheComponents: true`, `partialPrefetching: true`. `AGENTS.md` is written by Next (`next dev` re-adds it), so it is committed.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\backlog\\T3-cline-agent.md","result":" 1 | # T3: Cline SDK agent inside the product: Rule Maintenance Agent (about 75 min)\n 2 | \n 3 | Mode: PLAN first (short), then ACT. The bonus criterion; it must do a real, visible job.\n 4 | \n 5 | 1. `src/server/store.ts` (the only DB writer, `node:sqlite`): table `rule_versions` (schemeId, version, ruleJson, testsJson, testResultJson, status proposed|published|rejected, sourceNote, createdAt, approvedAt). On startup and on publish, load the latest published version of each scheme into the registry. Built-in schemes are version 1.\n 6 | 2. `src/server/agents/ruleMaintenance.ts`: `@cline/sdk` `Agent` (config in .clinerules/03-stack.md), tools via `createTool` with zod inputs:\n 7 |    - `getRuleSchema()` → the SchemeRule JSON schema + examples.\n 8 |    - `getCurrentRule(schemeId)` → the current published rule + its regression tests.\n 9 |    - `proposeRule(rule)` → zod validation errors, or ok.\n10 |    - `runTests(rule, testCases[])` → runs the new cases AND all existing regression tests for that scheme through `evaluate`/`benefitOn`; returns pass/fail per case.\n11 |    - `saveProposal(rule, tests, sourceNote)` → stores status `proposed`.\n12 |    System prompt: read the notice; decide whether it's a new scheme or a change to an existing one; propose the smallest rule change with provenance (sourceUrl if given, clause, effectiveDate; status `provisional` unless an official URL is provided); write regression tests; iterate until valid and all tests pass; never invent criteria not in the text (unclear → `notes`).\n13 | 3. API: `POST /api/admin/rules/propose` (notice text → run the agent, stream tool-call events), `GET /api/admin/rules`, `POST /api/admin/rules/:id/publish`, `POST /api/admin/rules/:id/reject`.\n14 | 4. UI `/admin`: paste box → live agent log (each tool call) → **readable diff** (old vs new values) → test results ✓/✗ (new + regression) → Publish / Reject. Version history list per scheme.\n15 | 5. Unit tests for the tools and store with a mocked agent (no network).\n16 | \n17 | **Done when:** (a) `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` → a valid Old Age Pension scheme with ≥3 passing tests; publishing makes it selectable; (b) `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` → a new Orunodoi version with an October override, tests showing 1500 in Oct / 1250 in Nov, and all old Orunodoi tests still passing. Tests and build pass; committed \"T3: Cline SDK rule maintenance agent\".","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\LOG.md","result":"  1 | # Build log (Cline appends after every task)\n  2 | \n  3 | ## T0: scaffold + memory bank (run-133358-c1ef, 2026-10-10)\n  4 | Followed the plan from run-133031-4cma.\n  5 | \n  6 | **Files created/changed**\n  7 | - Memory Bank: `memory-bank/productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `techContext.md`, `activeContext.md`, `progress.md` (`projectbrief.md` untouched).\n  8 | - Scaffold (create-next-app@16.4.0 in a temp folder, copied in): `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `tsconfig.json` (strict), `next.config.ts`, `eslint.config.mjs` (+ ignores for `.cline-runs/`, `docs/`, `memory-bank/`, `tasks/`), `next-env.d.ts`, `AGENTS.md`, `public/*`, `src/app/{layout.tsx,page.tsx,globals.css,favicon.ico}`.\n  9 | - New: `src/core/appInfo.ts` (title/taglines, pure), `src/core/appInfo.test.ts` (smoke test, also exercises zod + fast-check), `vitest.config.mts`, `.env.example` (`CLINE_API_KEY=`, `CLINE_MODEL=`), `README.md` (short placeholder), `.gitignore` (ignores `.env`, `.env*.local`, `node_modules`, `.next`, `*.db*`; keeps `.env.example` and `.cline-runs/`).\n 10 | - Deps added: `zod@^4.6.5`, dev `vitest@^5.0.3`, `fast-check@^4.10.2`, `@types/node@^22`.\n 11 | - Scripts: `dev`, `build`, `start`, `lint` (`eslint .`), `typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`), `test` (`vitest run`), `test:watch`.\n 12 | \n 13 | **Results**\n 14 | - `npm test`: 1 file, 3 passed, 0 failed.\n 15 | - `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass (0 problems). `npm run build`: pass (Next 16.4.0, Turbopack; `/` prerendered static).\n 16 | - Verified the built HTML contains \"KaagazCheck: कागज़ चेक\" and `lang=\"hi\"`, and the CSS contains the Tailwind utilities used.\n 17 | \n 18 | **Deviations from the plan**\n 19 | - `@types/node` bumped from `^20` to `^22` (Vitest 5 peer requirement; matches Node 22+).\n 20 | - Vitest config is `.mts` instead of `.ts` (avoids a Vite ESM/CJS config warning).\n 21 | - `layout.tsx` uses explicit `Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>` instead of the generated global `LayoutProps<\"/\">`, so `typecheck` passes before `.next/types` exists.\n 22 | - No `postcss.config.mjs`: create-next-app 16.4 wires Tailwind v4 via the `@tailwindcss/turbopack` loader in `next.config.ts`; Tailwind confirmed working in the build.\n 23 | \n 24 | **Open issues**\n 25 | - npm warns `eslint@9` is deprecated (pinned by eslint-config-next 16.4.0) and that `unrs-resolver` has an unapproved postinstall script; neither blocks lint or build.\n 26 | - `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` appeared in `docs/` during this run (not created by Cline); committed as-is with `git add -A`.\n 27 | \n 28 | **Requests for Claude**\n 29 | - None blocking. Please confirm that `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` is intended for T4 (rejection decoder) and reference it in the task spec if so.\n 30 | \n 31 | ## T1: core rule engine v2 (run-134715-f3yl, 2026-10-10)\n 32 | Followed `tasks/NEXT.md` (Step 0 + `tasks/backlog/T1-core-engine.md`), with `docs/schemes.md` v2 as the source of truth. I wrote the tests first: all new test files were written before the implementations, and the Step 0 smoke tests failed until `appInfo.ts` was updated.\n 33 | \n 34 | **Step 0**\n 35 | - Memory bank: `productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `activeContext.md` rewritten for brief v2 (two verdicts, provenance, Assamese). `progress.md` and `techContext.md` updated.\n 36 | - `src/core/appInfo.ts`: `APP_TITLE` \"KaagazCheck: কাগজ চেক\", `APP_TAGLINE_EN` \"Check before you apply\", `APP_TAGLINE_AS` \"আবেদনৰ আগতে পৰীক্ষা কৰক\", `APP_LANG = \"as\"`, and a longer `APP_DESCRIPTION_EN` for meta. `layout.tsx` uses `lang={APP_LANG}`; `page.tsx` shows the Assamese tagline first. The smoke test checks the exact title and taglines, Assamese ৰ (U+09F0) rather than Bengali র, and `lang`.\n 37 | \n 38 | **Files created (all pure, in `src/core/`)**\n 39 | - `types.ts`: zod schemas `RuleProvenance`, `SchemeRule` (with `version`), `ExtractedDoc`, `Answers`, `Question`, `DocRequirement`, `NameCheckRule`, `FieldCheckRule`, `ExternalCheckRule`, `AgeRange`, `Benefit` (+ `BenefitOverride`), `Check`, `Report`, `BenefitOn`.\n 40 | - `schemes/sources.ts` (provenance builders, verifiedOn 2026-10-10), `schemes/pm-kisan.ts`, `schemes/orunodoi-3.ts`, `schemes/nsap-widow.ts`, `schemes/index.ts` (`getScheme`, `listSchemes`, `listSchemeVersions`, `registerScheme`, `questionsFor`).\n 41 | - `nameMatch.ts` (+ `transliterate.ts`: Devanagari and Assamese/Bengali → Latin), `age.ts`, `aadhaar.ts`, `benefit.ts`, `evaluate.ts`, `rejectionCodes.ts`, `labels.ts`, `samples.ts` (fake samples A/B/C), `dates.ts`.\n 42 | - Tests: `nameMatch.test.ts`, `age.test.ts`, `aadhaar.test.ts`, `benefit.test.ts`, `evaluate.test.ts`, `rejectionCodes.test.ts`, `schemes/schemes.test.ts`.\n 43 | \n 44 | **Results**\n 45 | - `npm test`: 8 files, **93 passed, 0 failed** (including fast-check properties: same-as-itself, symmetry, mask ≤ 4 digits, possible_match never ok, Orunodoi never not_eligible, deterministic + schema-valid report, readiness invariant).\n 46 | - `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass. `npm run build`: pass. The built HTML has `lang=\"as\"`, the Assamese title and both taglines, and no Devanagari.\n 47 | - Required name cases and their scores: same (1) / same (1) / possible_match (0.999) / possible_match (0.999) / initials_only (0.875) / mismatch (0.644) / mismatch (0.778).\n 48 | - Samples on 2026-10-10: A → likely_eligible + ready_for_review (4 external checks need verification). B → action_required (bank possible_match, land mismatch). C → action_required (death certificate missing).\n 49 | \n 50 | **Design decisions / interpretations (please review)**\n 51 | - **Readiness with external checks:** external checks are always `needs_verification` but do not by themselves stop `ready_for_review`. This is needed for the T1 spec \"clean → ready_for_review with bank seeding as needs_verification\". Any other `needs_verification` (possible match, initials, low confidence < 0.8, provisional criterion, unanswered question) → readiness `needs_verification`.\n 52 | - **A verified criterion that fails** (e.g. income tax payer) → eligibility `not_eligible` and readiness `action_required`.\n 53 | - **Name `same`** means identical after formatting (case, punctuation, spaces, joined words, leading honorifics), compared in the original script. Any cross-script comparison is at best `possible_match`. The score is capped at 0.999 for anything that is not `same`. `possible_match` also covers reordered words and \"every word pair Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85\". A missing or extra word is a `mismatch` (so \"Rameshwar Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\" is a mismatch).\n 54 | - **Honorifics** are dropped only when they lead the name, so \"Sunita Kumari\" keeps KUMARI as a surname.\n 55 | - **PM-KISAN land owner:** a mismatch becomes `needs_verification` (never ok) if the user answers `land_in_family_member_name` = yes. docs/schemes.md allows \"applicant (or a family member) as owner\". The relationship can't be proven from a photo.\n 56 | - **Orunodoi** name checks use the ration card as the reference. Provisional questions are `nfsa_enrolled`, an any-of list and 7 exclusions. \"None of the any-of conditions\" → `needs_verification`. `ration_card_valid` is an external check.\n 57 | - **Widow pension** mandatory docs include `bpl_proof`, all provisional (docs/schemes.md: \"commonly required; confirm locally\"). A DOB that is low-confidence, unreadable or missing → age `needs_verification`, never `not_eligible`.\n 58 | - `RuleProvenance.sourceUrl` is nullable for provisional rules (needed for the T3 Orunodoi override \"provisional until an official notice URL is added\"). A schema refine stops a `verified` rule from having a null URL.\n 59 | - `benefitOn`: overrides are inclusive date windows and the last match wins. `total` is null when `stateTopUp` is null.\n 60 | - The registry is in-memory and keeps old versions. `getScheme(id)` returns the newest version; `getScheme(id, version)` returns that version.\n 61 | \n 62 | **Open issues**\n 63 | - All Assamese strings (scheme questions, labels, check messages, rejection fix steps, tagline) are drafts and need native-speaker review (Das).\n 64 | - The transliteration table is basic (no conjunct special cases beyond virama; schwa deletion only at word end).\n 65 | - The registry test registers `nsap-widow@2.1.0` in the shared in-memory registry. Vitest isolates test files, so other files are unaffected.\n 66 | \n 67 | **Requests for Claude**\n 68 | - Please confirm the readiness rule for external checks (they don't block `ready_for_review` on their own), or say if you want a different label, e.g. `ready_for_review` with a \"confirm these N items\" list. T2's UI will show them as a separate \"confirm at bank/portal\" group.\n 69 | - Please confirm the Orunodoi any-of list and the widow pension `bpl_proof` document are wanted as modelled.\n 70 | \n 71 | \n 72 | ## T2: main flow (run-144641-b8cr, 2026-10-10)\n 73 | Followed `tasks/NEXT.md` (T2 + adjustments) and `tasks/backlog/T2-main-flow.md`. I wrote tests first for every new pure module and for both API routes. One mobile flow: scheme → documents → confirm fields → questions → two-verdict report → print cover sheet.\n 74 | \n 75 | **Files created**\n 76 | - Pure core (tested): `src/core/extraction.ts` (raw model JSON → strict `ExtractedDoc`; DD/MM/YYYY → ISO; full Aadhaar → last 4 digits; AI-read fields without a score get confidence 0.5 so they are always confirmed), `src/core/docFields.ts` (which fields each doc type needs), `src/core/flow.ts` (document slots, field edit/confirm, upsert/remove, relevant answers), `src/core/reportView.ts` (fix / verify / external / ok sections, 🟢🔴🟡⚪ tones, `₹1,25,000` formatting, benefit view), `src/core/catalog.ts` (serialisable scheme list, PM-KISAN first as flagship), `src/core/thresholds.ts`.\n 77 | - `src/i18n.ts`: all fixed UI strings, `as` (default) + `en`, same keys (tested), with doc/office names reused from `labels.ts`.\n 78 | - `src/server/ai.ts`: the only model caller. Cline API chat/completions with an `image_url` part, then JSON extraction, zod `RawExtraction`, `toExtractedDoc`, one retry, then `{ error }` (`ai_unavailable` | `ai_failed` | `invalid_image`). `fetch`/`env`/`log` are injectable for tests. Logs `{ model, promptVersion: \"extract-doc-v1\", inputHash (sha256/16), attempt, outcome, ms }` only.\n 79 | - `src/server/api.ts` + `src/app/api/check/route.ts`, `src/app/api/extract/route.ts` (thin). `/api/check` validates with zod (strict `ExtractedDoc`, so a full Aadhaar is rejected), 404 for an unknown scheme/version, `asOfDate` defaults to today in IST. Error bodies hold only paths and codes, never submitted values.\n 80 | - UI (`src/app/_components/`): `KaagazApp` (state + steps), `SchemeStep`, `DocsStep` (photo per slot with camera capture, browser downscale to JPEG ≤1600px, \"type it in\", samples A/B/C for the chosen scheme), `ConfirmStep` (low confidence highlighted in amber, \"This is correct\" button), `QuestionsStep` (big Yes/No, \"rule not confirmed\" badge), `ReportStep` + `CheckItem` + `BenefitCard`, `CoverSheet` (print only, masked Aadhaar, no account number), `ui.tsx`, `image.ts`.\n 81 | - `scripts/smoke.mjs`: manual smoke test against a running server (not part of `npm test`).\n 82 | - Tests: `src/core/{extraction,flow,reportView,catalog}.test.ts`, `src/i18n.test.ts`, `src/server/{ai,apiCheck,apiExtract}.test.ts` (ai.ts mocked in the API tests; `fetch` injected in the ai tests; no network).\n 83 | \n 84 | **Files changed**\n 85 | - `src/app/page.tsx` (server component → `KaagazApp` with the catalog + samples), `src/app/layout.tsx` (Noto Sans Bengali for Assamese, viewport, Geist Mono dropped), `src/app/globals.css` (one light high-contrast theme, font stack, print background).\n 86 | - `src/core/evaluate.ts`: `LOW_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` moved to `thresholds.ts` and re-exported, so the client bundle doesn't pull in the engine.\n 87 | \n 88 | **Results**\n 89 | - `npm test`: 16 files, 150 passed, 0 failed (93 from T1 + 57 new).\n 90 | - `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass. `npm run build`: pass (`/` static, `/api/check` + `/api/extract` dynamic).\n 91 | - Smoke test on `next start`: home HTML has `lang=\"as\"`, the Assamese title and the flagship badge. `/api/check` A → likely_eligible + ready_for_review (4 external checks to verify); B → action_required (`name_land_record` action_required, `name_bank_passbook` possible_match → verify); C → action_required (`doc_death_certificate`).\n 92 | - Live AI check with the real key (fake \"SAMPLE ONLY\" Aadhaar image I drew locally): 200, `{ name: \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\", dob: \"1975-03-12\", aadhaarLast4: \"4821\" }` from the printed \"1234 5678 4821\". Image input is accepted by the Cline API. With no key: 503 `ai_unavailable`, and the UI switches to manual entry.\n 93 | \n 94 | \n 95 | **Design decisions / deviations (please review)**\n 96 | - **No `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"` in the route files.** Next 16.4 fails the build with \"Route segment config \"runtime\" is not compatible with `nextConfig.cacheComponents`\". Node.js is the default (and the only runtime with cacheComponents), so the routes do run on Node. A comment in each route explains this. Rule 03-stack asks for the export, so please confirm.\n 97 | - **The Cline API wraps the OpenAI body as `{ data: { choices } }`.** `ai.ts` accepts both shapes (tested). Before this fix, every live call fell back to `ai_failed`.\n 98 | - **Environment gotcha:** this shell has an empty `CLINE_MODEL` environment variable. Next does not override an existing env var from `.env.local`, so the server saw no model and returned `ai_unavailable`. It works after `Remove-Item Env:CLINE_MODEL`. Added to techContext.\n 99 | - **Minimum data:** nothing is read from the death certificate or BPL proof (the engine only checks that they are present), so `husbandName` is not collected. The cover sheet shows the masked Aadhaar and no account number.\n100 | - **Empty manual docs:** \"Type it in\" adds the document with empty fields. The engine then counts it as present, and its fields show as \"please verify\"/\"could not read\". I think this is right (\"I have it, I'll type it\"); flagging it in case you prefer the slot to count only once a field is filled.\n101 | - A sample replaces any documents and answers already entered and jumps to \"Check what we read\" (all sample fields are ≥ 0.8 confidence, so nothing is highlighted). The purple \"Demo mode: fake sample documents (A)\" label stays on every step and on the printed sheet.\n102 | - Unanswered questions are allowed; the engine marks them needs_verification (a note under the questions says so).\n103 | \n104 | **Open issues**\n105 | - All new Assamese UI strings in `src/i18n.ts` are drafts and need native-speaker review (Das), like the T1 strings.\n106 | - I did not test the UI in a real phone browser here (no browser automation in this environment). The flow was checked through the built HTML and the APIs; a manual click-through on a phone is recommended before the demo.\n107 | - `tasks/NEXT.md` (Claude's T2 spec), `.cline-runs/index.md` and `run-134715-f3yl.log` were already modified before this run, not by me. They are committed as-is with `git add -A`, per the workflow; I did not edit them.\n108 | \n109 | **Requests for Claude**\n110 | - Confirm dropping `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"` (see above), or say whether to turn off `cacheComponents` instead.\n111 | - Confirm that \"Type it in\" should mark a document as added before any field is filled.\n112 | ","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\docs\\sample-guideline-ignoaps.md","result":" 1 | # Sample input for the Scheme Onboarding Agent (demo)\n 2 | \n 3 | *Paste this text into the admin \"Add a scheme\" page. Summary of the Indira Gandhi National Old Age Pension Scheme (IGNOAPS) under NSAP. Source: https://en.vikaspedia.in/viewcontent/social-welfare/social-security/pension-benefits-under-nsap?lgn=en*\n 4 | \n 5 | ---\n 6 | \n 7 | Indira Gandhi National Old Age Pension Scheme (IGNOAPS), a component of the National Social Assistance Programme, Ministry of Rural Development.\n 8 | \n 9 | Eligibility: The applicant must be aged 60 years or above and must belong to a household living below the poverty line (BPL) according to the criteria prescribed by the Government of India.\n10 | \n11 | Central assistance: Rs. 200 per month for beneficiaries aged 60 to 79 years, and Rs. 500 per month for beneficiaries aged 80 years and above. State governments are urged to contribute an additional amount.\n12 | \n13 | Documents generally required: Aadhaar card (age proof), BPL proof, bank account passbook.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\docs\\sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md","result":" 1 | # Sample input for the Rule Maintenance Agent: a temporary payment change (demo)\n 2 | \n 3 | *Demo notice modelled on a reported October 2026 change (The Economic Times report of a one-time ₹1,500 Orunodoi payment for that month). Before quoting on slides, confirm against the official Government of Assam notification.*\n 4 | \n 5 | ---\n 6 | \n 7 | Orunodoi: For the month of October 2026, eligible beneficiaries will receive a one-time amount of Rs. 1,500 instead of the regular Rs. 1,250. From November 2026, the regular monthly amount of Rs. 1,250 continues.\n 8 | \n 9 | ---\n10 | \n11 | Expected agent behaviour: propose a new version of `orunodoi-3` with a time-bounded benefit override (effective 2026-10-01 to 2026-10-31, amount 1500), keep the recurring 1250, mark provenance as provisional until an official notice URL is added, write regression tests (October date → 1500, November date → 1250, eligibility checks unchanged), run all existing tests, and wait for human approval.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\README.md","result":"1 | # tasks/\n2 | - `NEXT.md` — the one task Cline does next (written by Claude).\n3 | - `backlog/` — the day's tasks. T0 and T-last are ready; Claude writes T1–T4 after reading the problem statement.\n4 | - `LOG.md` — Cline's report after each task.","success":true}],"durationMs":9}}
