n49 | \n50 | **Design decisions / interpretations (please review)**\n51 | - **Readiness with external checks:** external checks are always `needs_verification` but do not by themselves stop `ready_for_review`. This is needed for the T1 spec \"clean → ready_for_review with bank seeding as needs_verification\". Any other `needs_verification` (possible match, initials, low confidence < 0.8, provisional criterion, unanswered question) → readiness `needs_verification`.\n52 | - **A verified criterion that fails** (e.g. income tax payer) → eligibility `not_eligible` and readiness `action_required`.\n53 | - **Name `same`** means identical after formatting (case, punctuation, spaces, joined words, leading honorifics), compared in the original script. Any cross-script comparison is at best `possible_match`. The score is capped at 0.999 for anything that is not `same`. `possible_match` also covers reordered words and \"every word pair Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85\". A missing or extra word is a `mismatch` (so \"Rameshwar Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\" is a mismatch).\n54 | - **Honorifics** are dropped only when they lead the name, so \"Sunita Kumari\" keeps KUMARI as a surname.\n55 | - **PM-KISAN land owner:** a mismatch becomes `needs_verification` (never ok) if the user answers `land_in_family_member_name` = yes. docs/schemes.md allows \"applicant (or a family member) as owner\". The relationship can't be proven from a photo.\n56 | - **Orunodoi** name checks use the ration card as the reference. Provisional questions are `nfsa_enrolled`, an any-of list and 7 exclusions. \"None of the any-of conditions\" → `needs_verification`. `ration_card_valid` is an external check.\n57 | - **Widow pension** mandatory docs include `bpl_proof`, all provisional (docs/schemes.md: \"commonly required; confirm locally\"). A DOB that is low-confidence, unreadable or missing → age `needs_verification`, never `not_eligible`.\n58 | - `RuleProvenance.sourceUrl` is nullable for provisional rules (needed for the T3 Orunodoi override \"provisional until an official notice URL is added\"). A schema refine stops a `verified` rule from having a null URL.\n59 | - `benefitOn`: overrides are inclusive date windows and the last match wins. `total` is null when `stateTopUp` is null.\n60 | - The registry is in-memory and keeps old versions. `getScheme(id)` returns the newest version; `getScheme(id, version)` returns that version.\n61 | \n62 | **Open issues**\n63 | - All Assamese strings (scheme questions, labels, check messages, rejection fix steps, tagline) are drafts and need native-speaker review (Das).\n64 | - The transliteration table is basic (no conjunct special cases beyond virama; schwa deletion only at word end).\n65 | - The registry test registers `nsap-widow@2.1.0` in the shared in-memory registry. Vitest isolates test files, so other files are unaffected.\n66 | \n67 | **Requests for Claude**\n68 | - Please confirm the readiness rule for external checks (they don't block `ready_for_review` on their own), or say if you want a different label, e.g. `ready_for_review` with a \"confirm these N items\" list. T2's UI will show them as a separate \"confirm at bank/portal\" group.\n69 | - Please confirm the Orunodoi any-of list and the widow pension `bpl_proof` document are wanted as modelled.\n70 | \n71 | \n72 | ## T2: main flow (run-144641-b8cr, 2026-10-10)\n73 | Followed `tasks/NEXT.md` (T2 + adjustments) and `tasks/backlog/T2-main-flow.md`. I wrote tests first for every new pure module and for both API routes. One mobile flow: scheme → documents → confirm fields → questions → two-verdict report → print cover sheet.\n74 | \n75 | **Files created**\n76 | - Pure core (tested): `src/core/extraction.ts` (raw model JSON → strict `ExtractedDoc`; DD/MM/YYYY → ISO; full Aadhaar → last 4 digits; AI-read fields without a score get confidence 0.5 so they are always confirmed), `src/core/docFields.ts` (which fields each doc type needs), `src/core/flow.ts` (document slots, field edit/confirm, upsert/remove, relevant answers), `src/core/reportView.ts` (fix / verify / external / ok sections, 🟢🔴🟡⚪ tones, `₹1,25,000` formatting, benefit view), `src/core/catalog.ts` (serialisable scheme list, PM-KISAN first as flagship), `src/core/thresholds.ts`.\n77 | - `src/i18n.ts`: all fixed UI strings, `as` (default) + `en`, same keys (tested), with doc/office names reused from `labels.ts`.\n78 | - `src/server/ai.ts`: the only model caller. Cline API chat/completions with an `image_url` part, then JSON extraction, zod `RawExtraction`, `toExtractedDoc`, one retry, then `{ error }` (`ai_unavailable` | `ai_failed` | `invalid_image`). `fetch`/`env`/`log` are injectable for tests. Logs `{ model, promptVersion: \"extract-doc-v1\", inputHash (sha256/16), attempt, outcome, ms }` only.\n79 | - `src/server/api.ts` + `src/app/api/check/route.ts`, `src/app/api/extract/route.ts` (thin). `/api/check` validates with zod (strict `ExtractedDoc`, so a full Aadhaar is rejected), 404 for an unknown scheme/version, `asOfDate` defaults to today in IST. Error bodies hold only paths and codes, never submitted values.\n80 | - UI (`src/app/_components/`): `KaagazApp` (state + steps), `SchemeStep`, `DocsStep` (photo per slot with camera capture, browser downscale to JPEG ≤1600px, \"type it in\", samples A/B/C for the chosen scheme), `ConfirmStep` (low confidence highlighted in amber, \"This is correct\" button), `QuestionsStep` (big Yes/No, \"rule not confirmed\" badge), `ReportStep` + `CheckItem` + `BenefitCard`, `CoverSheet` (print only, masked Aadhaar, no account number), `ui.tsx`, `image.ts`.\n81 | - `scripts/smoke.mjs`: manual smoke test against a running server (not part of `npm test`).\n82 | - Tests: `src/core/{extraction,flow,reportView,catalog}.test.ts`, `src/i18n.test.ts`, `src/server/{ai,apiCheck,apiExtract}.test.ts` (ai.ts mocked in the API tests; `fetch` injected in the ai tests; no network).\n83 | \n84 | **Files changed**\n85 | - `src/app/page.tsx` (server component → `KaagazApp` with the catalog + samples), `src/app/layout.tsx` (Noto Sans Bengali for Assamese, viewport, Geist Mono dropped), `src/app/globals.css` (one light high-contrast theme, font stack, print background).\n86 | - `src/core/evaluate.ts`: `LOW_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` moved to `thresholds.ts` and re-exported, so the client bundle doesn't pull in the engine.","success":true}],"durationMs":2}}
