{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:58:08.167Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm thinking through a design where a document only counts as \"added\" once its main field has a value—mapping doc types to their primary field name and checking if it's filled. But I'm stuck on doc types like death_certificate or bpl_proof that don't have a field to type into at all, so I need to figure out what \"added\" even means for those.\n\nFor fieldless docs, I'll treat them as counted the moment they're added rather than requiring text entry, since there's nothing to type. I need to map out each doc type's main field (aadhaar→name, bank_passbook→name, land_record→ownerNames, ration_card→name, etc.), then decide where to apply this filtering—likely creating a `countedDocs` helper used both when sending data to /api/check and when determining which slots show as \"added\" in DocsStep, while still keeping uncounted docs visible in ConfirmStep for typing.\n\nI'll keep the core engine's presence semantics untouched since changing it risks breaking existing tests, and instead handle this counting logic entirely in the client flow layer. I still need to check ConfirmStep and the i18n strings for \"Type it in\" to see if no-field docs should get a different label like \"I have it\".\n\nFor the bigger task, I need to install @cline/sdk and check its API—let me first see if it's already present in node_modules before kicking off a potentially slow npm install.\n\n"}}
