{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:58:30.826Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"While that installs, I'll tackle fix #1 so \"type it in\" only counts once the main field has a value, starting with a test. I'm designing a pure helper that maps each doc type to its main field and filters documents by whether that field is filled, while handling edge cases like doc types with no fields at all where \"added\" needs different logic.\n\nDeath certificate and bpl_proof have no fields, so I'll treat them as counted immediately on presence alone, since there's nothing to type for them. I'm mapping main fields per type (aadhaar→name, land_record→ownerNames, etc.) and now weighing whether this filtering logic should live purely client-side in flow.ts or also change the engine itself, since altering the engine's doc-matching could affect existing sample outcomes.\n\nBut I need to check whether existing evaluate tests use docs with empty fields, since changing findDoc could break presence-only checks like death certificates. I'll make the engine authoritative with a shared helper, then look at evaluate's logic and grep the tests to confirm nothing breaks.\n\n"}}
