{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:58:45.192Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm thinking through how to handle docs with no fillable fields, like death certificates or birthplace proof—since there's nothing to \"type in,\" I'll treat those as counted once marked present rather than requiring a field value.\n\nI'm weighing whether to enforce this \"has-value\" rule only at the UI level or also inside the core engine, since the engine should be the authority on outcomes and shouldn't let the API be bypassed—so I'm leaning toward building this check into the engine's evaluation logic itself, filtering which docs qualify before any mandatory-doc matching happens.\n\nThat said, I'm worried this could break existing tests, like ones where a doc has a missing name and currently triggers \"could not read the name\" instead of being treated as absent—so I want to check the evaluate test cases to see how many rely on that nameless-doc behavior before deciding.\n\nI'll add a pure `MAIN_FIELD` map and `isDocAdded(doc)` in core so presence-only docs like death certificates count as added immediately, then use it across the UI badge, missing-required count, and `/api/check`. First I'll check whether engine tests rely on nameless documents before deciding if the engine should enforce this too.\n\n"}}
