{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:59:03.349Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"While the install continues, I'm thinking through the fix: a document should only count as \"added\" once its name field has an actual value, so I need to filter out documents missing the main field before they're sent to the check endpoint, and have the docs step only show \"added\" status once that field is populated.\n\nFor documents like death_certificate and bpl_proof that have no fields to fill in, presence itself should count as added since there's nothing to type. I'm also weighing whether the engine should enforce this too — being defensive about empty main fields reaching the check endpoint — but worry that AI extraction might legitimately fail to read a name from a blurry photo even when the document is genuinely present.\n\nI'll keep that enforcement in the pure flow layer instead, using a MAIN_FIELD mapping and isDocAdded/addedDocs helpers, so DocsStep shows the right badges and KaagazApp sends the filtered set to /api/check and CoverSheet, while ConfirmStep still lets users fill in drafts. For the DocsStep button logic, I'm distinguishing between documents fully added, documents merely drafted, and documents not yet started, with status text guiding the user to \"type the details\" when needed.\n\nI'm also weighing whether to enforce the same filtering server-side — applying addedDocs before evaluate in handleCheck — so the decision logic isn't purely client-trusted, while keeping isDocAdded for client-side display only. Sending draft docs to the server is harmless either way, so I'll centralize the filtering on the server and use the client version just for UI state.\n\nNext I should check CoverSheet's rendering of docs and the i18n strings for doc labels to make sure drafts aren't shown there either.\n\n"}}
