{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:59:22.632Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm thinking through how to define when a document counts as \"added\" - probably needing a helper that checks whether the document's main identifying field (like name, or ownerNames for land records) has a value, though presence-only docs without fields complicate this.\n\nFor documents without a specific field (like death certificates), I'll treat them as counted once added since presence alone is the only requirement. Then I need to filter which docs get sent to the check API to only include those meeting this \"added\" criteria, and update the DocsStep UI to distinguish between truly added docs versus pending ones still needing a name typed in - though I'm wary that enforcing this filter at the engine level could change existing behavior, like cases where AI reads a document's DOB but not its name.\n\nThe safer approach is keeping the engine as-is and adding a pure filtering function client-side, so the confirm step still shows blank docs to the user for typing while the check API only receives properly completed ones. I'm now mapping out which field counts as the \"main\" field for each document type - name for aadhaar and bank passbook, owner names for land records, null for death certificates and BPL proof - and organizing this logic into a dedicated fields file alongside a helper function for determining if a doc counts as added.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the app wiring: the check flow and cover sheet should both use the filtered docs list, while the docs step itself needs three distinct states - added, pending (meaning the user still needs to type the name on the next screen), and not added - with the remove button staying visible for both added and pending docs. I'll need a new translation string for the pending state, so let me check the existing i18n file for the docs section while I wait on the SDK installation to look into its API.\n\n"}}
