{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:59:39.007Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"With the install finished, I'll check the SDK's README and type definitions next. For the \"type it in\" fix, I'm defining that a document counts as added once its main field has a value, except for doc types like death_certificate and bpl_proof that have no fields at all—those should just be treated as added immediately since there's nothing to type.\n\nI'm weighing where to filter: adding a helper to check if a doc is \"added\" and applying it before sending data to the check API and in the DocsStep logic, while still letting \"Type it in\" create the blank doc so the Confirm step can show its fields. The real question is whether this filtering should happen client-side only, or also inside the engine itself so an API client sending empty docs wouldn't count them—but I'm wary that pushing it into the engine could break existing evaluate test fixtures that may have docs lacking names.\n\nI decide it's safer to keep the engine unchanged and only filter in the flow layer, with a corresponding flow.test.ts addition—this is the minimal, lower-risk change. I'm also mapping out which field counts as the \"main field\" for each doc type: name for most types, ownerNames for land_record, and null (presence-only) for death_certificate and bpl_proof.\n\n"}}
