{"ts":"2026-10-10T10:01:31.812Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"The AgentModel interface letting me inject a scripted fake model for offline tests is a solid approach, since it drives the real Agent loop through tools. Now I'm wondering whether @cline/sdk imports cleanly in a Next.js server build given its ESM and heavy dependencies, so I should verify that with a quick Node import test.\n\nI also need to check if \"openai-compatible\" is a valid providerId, and confirm zod versions align between shared and root packages so schema conversion works without conflicts. Given the stack rules point to @cline/sdk, I'll import Agent and createTool from there despite the heavier bundle, though I should still test import time and verify the provider ID list.\n\nThe SDK's AgentModel interface lets me inject a scripted fake model to drive the real Agent loop and tools fully offline in tests. Next I'll verify the SDK imports under Node, find valid provider IDs, and check how createTool converts zod schemas to JSON schema.\n\n"}}
