{"ts":"2026-10-10T10:04:34.998Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"Good, the live probe confirms the Agent with openai-compatible tool calling works against the Cline API, and node:sqlite works too. Now I'm turning to the Next.js docs, thinking through dynamic route params being Promises in Next 16, and whether GET handlers with cacheComponents need an explicit connection() call to avoid being statically prerendered.\n\nWith cacheComponents enabled, the home page reading `listSchemes()` would get prerendered as static at build time, which breaks the requirement that published versions take effect immediately -- so I need to make it dynamic, likely via `connection()` inside a Suspense boundary, and I should check the cacheComponents, connection, route, serverExternalPackages, and streaming docs. I'm also considering whether `@cline/sdk`, being a large ESM package potentially with native dependencies, should be added to `serverExternalPackages`.\n\nConfirmed the live probe works—Agent with the openai-compatible provider correctly returns tool calls via the Cline API, and `node:sqlite` is available. Next I'll review Next.js 16 docs on route handlers with dynamic params, `connection()`/dynamic rendering under `cacheComponents`, streaming responses, and `serverExternalPackages` to cover T3's dependencies.\n\n"}}
