{"ts":"2026-10-10T10:12:11.678Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_start","contentType":"text","text":" **U","accumulated":"I have the context I need. Here is the plan before I write code.\n\n## Plan (T3 + the small fix)\n\n**What I found in `@cline/sdk` 0.0.92.** It only re-exports `@cline/core`, which re-exports `Agent` from `@cline/agents` and `createTool` from `@cline/shared`. Details that matter:\n- `new Agent({ providerId: \"openai-compatible\", baseUrl, apiKey, modelId, systemPrompt, tools, maxIterations })`, then `agent.run(text)` returns `{ status, outputText, iterations }`.\n- `agent.subscribe()` emits `tool-started` / `tool-finished` / `assistant-message` / `run-failed` events.\n- `createTool({ name, description, inputSchema: zod, execute })` converts zod to JSON Schema.\n- A live probe against the Cline API called a tool correctly (17+25 → 42 in 2.6 s).\n\n**0. Small fix (\"type it in\").** Add `MAIN_FIELD` per doc type, plus `isDocAdded` / `countedDocs` in `flow.ts` (written test-first). The UI shows \"details still to type\", and only counted docs go to `/api/check` and onto the cover sheet. Doc types that hold no fields (death certificate, BPL proof) count as soon as they are added.\n\n**T3 modules:**\n1. **Pure core:**\n   - `ruleTests.ts`: zod `RuleTestCase` (benefit / evaluate) and `runRuleTests`.\n   - `schemes/regression.ts`: the built-in regression suites.\n   - `ruleDiff.ts`: a readable before/after diff.\n   - `rulePolicy.ts`, enforced by code: the version must go up, and a `verified` provenance needs a URL from the notice or must be carried over unchanged.\n   - `notice.ts`: pulls the notice text out of the demo `.md` files.\n   - `agentLog.ts`: one-line summaries of each tool call.\n2. **`server/store.ts`:** the only DB writer. `node:sqlite`, WAL, transactions, a `rule_versions` table.\n3. **`server/rules.ts`:** syncs published versions into the registry (idempotent, on every request), and handles validate / test / save / publish / reject.\n4. **`server/ai.ts`:** gets `runToolAgent`, so the model calls still go through one module. It builds the `@cline/sdk` Agent, logs model / prompt version / input hash, retries once, then falls back to `{ error }`.\n5. **`server/agents/ruleMaintenance.ts`:** the 5 tools (zod inputs; tools only, no file writes) and the system prompt.\n6. **API:** a streaming NDJSON propose route, a list route, and publish / reject routes. **U"}}
