{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:02:53.864Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm realizing `connection()` needs an active request scope, so I'm weighing options like accepting a `req: Request` parameter to force dynamic rendering versus testing the handler logic directly, trying to avoid a hacky workaround.\n\nSince the synchronous sqlite driver could finish queries during prerendering regardless, the safer approach is to have the test call `handleList` directly rather than going through the route's GET, keeping `connection()` in the thin route wrapper and just updating the test accordingly.\n\nThe `connection()` call requires a real Next request scope that Vitest can't provide, but it's still needed to prevent Next from prerendering the GET route at build time. I'll have the test call `handleList` directly instead, keeping the route as a thin wrapper covered by the live smoke test.\n\n"}}
