{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:12:41.858Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"The Old Age Pension proposal looks valid and tested, satisfying Done-when (a), but I notice the server log shows attempt 1 ended in run_failed with only 2 tool calls, which is odd since more than zero tool calls usually means no retry happened. I need to check why the agent kept going despite that failure.\n\nThe regression test behavior on existing schemes looks correct, and the age-85 eligibility handling with the placeholder max of 120 is consistent with the source text. The ₹500 benefit for 80+ isn't modeled in the engine, which is a real gap I should flag as a limitation rather than silently ignore.\n\nNow waiting for the Orunodoi results to come through.\n\nThe Old Age Pension scheme passed all 5 tests, though I noted the ₹500 benefit for ages 80+ can't be computed by the engine and is only documented. Now waiting on the Orunodoi run to finish.\n\n"}}
