{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:13:32.018Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"Both demos worked end to end. I'm noticing an earlier run_failed log at 29.4s sharing the same input hash as the first OAP run — that came from my initial timed-out invocation where the client disconnected and the server marked the aborted run as failed, which is expected behavior, though I want to double-check the handling here.\n\nI'm catching an inconsistency: the comment in `send()` says to keep running so a valid proposal is saved, but the abort signal actually stops the agent when the client disconnects. Stopping on disconnect seems like the right behavior since the user clicked Stop, and since that first run only made 2 tool calls before aborting, it never reached saveProposal, so the DB still only has proposals #1 and #2 — I'll just fix the misleading comment. For the OAP new-scheme case, the agent correctly reported 0/0 regression tests since it's a new scheme, and the done-when criteria around ≥3 passing tests and publishing look satisfied, though I need to think through whether \"existing regression tests still pass\" even applies when there's no existing scheme to compare against.\n\nThe age-max placeholder was disclosed, so that's acceptable, and the flat-amount limitation for 80+ gets noted for Claude. On provenance, the provisional label for the Vikaspedia-sourced rule is appropriately conservative given the system prompt's strict \"verified only with official sourceUrl\" policy, even though it creates inconsistency with the existing nsap-widow entry — that's pre-existing data, not something to fix now. The mojibake is just console encoding, not a real issue, so now I want to manually verify the UI by fetching the admin page and homepage to confirm the buttons and scheme listing render correctly.\n\nI also want to double-check the smoke.db path didn't land somewhere unexpected before cleaning up and stopping the server, and I should tighten the abort-on-disconnect comment to clarify it means the client disconnected and the agent is being stopped. The getRuleSchema size and the 240s timeout versus actual 20-58s run times both look fine. Final step is checking the admin HTML render, then shutting down the server.\n\nBoth demo notices (IGNOAPS nsap-old-age 1.0.0 and Orunodoi 2.1.0) pass their tests end-to-end against the real Cline API, and the earlier `run_failed` log was just from a timed-out first invocation. Now I'll check the `/admin` HTML before stopping the server.\n\n"}}
