{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:14:25.688Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"My kill signal didn't actually match, so the server stayed up and returned 200 — I'll need to fix that later. More puzzling is the log showing two attempt-1 entries with the same inputHash but different outcomes and tool-call counts, which shouldn't happen since my code doesn't retry after tool calls occur and the smoke script only calls propose once.\n\nAh, I think I see it now — the first command that timed out at 30s was itself running the smoke script in the foreground. Killing that shell killed node mid-connection, which triggered the server's abort handling and logged it as run_failed with status aborted, while the proposal from that run never got saved since it only had 2 tool calls. That actually confirms the abort path works correctly, though it exposes a conflict: my handlePropose comment says to keep running after the client disconnects, but my code aborts on req.signal instead — I should keep the abort behavior for the stop-button use case and just fix the stale comment.\n\nThe agent's note about the 120 placeholder upper age is really it working around the schema requiring a max value; its summary flags this honestly, so it's acceptable for now, though I should note for later that the ageRange schema could make max optional. Time to properly kill the server by finding whatever process is listening on port 3123.\n\nBoth demo notices (Old Age Pension and Orunodoi) are verified end-to-end against the real Cline API, with publishing, overrides, and tests all passing correctly. The extra `run_failed` log was just a harmless aborted run from a timed-out first attempt, so now I'll stop the still-running server by its port.\n\n"}}
