{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:15:01.751Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"That first run_failed at 29s makes sense now — the 30s timeout killed the shell client mid-request, triggering an abort that logged as run_failed. That's correct behavior, worth noting in the log. I'm also seeing the agent flagged a concern about regression tests only running on changes to an existing scheme.\n\nSince a new scheme is independent of other rule packs, 0/0 regression is expected and fine, though it might be nice to eventually show whole-suite results. The agent was also honest about the ₹500 for 80+ limitation being unrepresentable — worth logging as a feature request, and it correctly referenced the widow pension scheme and self-corrected a wrong scheme id lookup during the Orunodoi run, which is fine behavior. I should clean up the temp log files like .build.log, .server.log, .agent-smoke.log, and .cline-install.log by deleting them.\n\nI also want to verify npm test, typecheck, lint, and build scripts run cleanly, but I notice that apiCheck tests can inadvertently create a real data/kaagaz.db file since they don't override KAAGAZ_DB_PATH like adminApi tests do — this could let a locally published scheme version bleed into test results. The cleaner fix is setting KAAGAZ_DB_PATH to ':memory:' in the vitest config environment, since the store already supports that special path.\n\nSince env vars are shared within a worker process, I should make the adminApi test restore the previous env value in afterEach rather than just deleting it, to avoid leaking state across test files. I'll also check whether data/kaagaz.db actually got created during the test run.\n\nThe live check passed and publishing updated the citizen API correctly; the earlier `run_failed` log entry was just my tool timeout, not a real agent failure. I noticed `/api/check` tests hit the real `data/kaagaz.db` via `getRuleService()`, so I'll fix that by pointing Vitest at an in-memory DB instead.\n\n"}}
