{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:18:15.344Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm confirming that createTool skips input validation, relying instead on the service layer to validate deeper structures—schemes via SchemeRule, tests via RuleTestCase arrays—while malformed outer shapes like non-string schemeId or non-array tests still get caught downstream by service methods like currentRule and runTests.\n\nFor saveProposal though, bad input like a non-string sourceNote would throw directly rather than being caught cleanly, just surfacing as an error tool result. It'd be better to validate explicitly upfront, so I'm planning to add a small `validated(schema, fn)` wrapper helper in ruleMaintenance.ts, plus a test confirming invalid input produces proper error output.\n\n"}}
