{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:19:23.089Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"editor","toolCallId":"toolu_01Xfz58Jo8wsQDzpD4y4XkJ5","output":{"query":"edit:C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\progress.md","result":"Edited C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\progress.md\n```diff\n-19: - Route files omit `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"` (incompatible with `cacheComponents` in Next 16.4); awaiting Claude's confirmation.\n+19: - Route files omit `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"` (incompatible with `cacheComponents` in Next 16.4); approved by Claude in T3.\n+20: - `/admin` has no authentication (anyone who can reach the server can run the agent and publish). Fine for the local demo; needs a decision before any deployment.\n+21: - The engine has one flat benefit amount per scheme, so IGNOAPS's ₹500/month for ages 80+ can only be a note (the agent said so itself). Age-banded benefits would need an engine change.\n+22: - A live agent run takes about 20–60 s; the UI streams each tool call so the wait is visible.\n+23: - `npm install` warns that `protobufjs` (a dependency of `@cline/sdk`) has an unapproved postinstall script. Harmless; nothing is broken.\n```","success":true},"durationMs":14}}
{"ts":"2026-10-10T11:19:23.090Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_start","contentType":"tool","toolName":"editor","toolCallId":"toolu_019P4STBJoMFDzD6d4UZ2Kfm","input":{"path":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\systemPatterns.md","old_text":"- `src/server/store.ts` (T3): the **only** database writer (`node:sqlite`, WAL, transactions); `rule_versions` table.\n- `src/server/agent/` (T3): `@cline/sdk` Rule Maintenance Agent; its tools call `src/core` (`registerScheme`, `evaluate`).","new_text":"- T3 pure core: `ruleTests.ts` (zod `RuleTestCase` benefit|evaluate + deterministic `runRuleTests`), `schemes/regression.ts` (built-in regression suites), `ruleDiff.ts` (keyed before/after diff), `ruleDiffView.ts` (plain-English labels for the UI), `rulePolicy.ts` (version bump, ≥ 3 new tests, verified-provenance rule), `mergePatch.ts` (RFC 7386), `notice.ts` (normalise; extract the demo notices), `agentLog.ts` (one-line tool summaries).\n- `src/server/store.ts` (T3): the **only** database writer (`node:sqlite`, WAL, every write in `BEGIN IMMEDIATE … COMMIT`); `rule_versions` table (+ `notice`, `summary`).\n- `src/server/rules.ts` (T3): `RuleService`: candidate (full rule or merge patch) → validate (zod + policy) → runTests (new + regression) → saveProposal (only if all pass) → publish (re-check, then `registerScheme`) / reject. `syncRegistry()` loads published versions into the registry (idempotent; called per request).\n- `src/server/agents/ruleMaintenance.ts` (T3): `@cline/sdk` Rule Maintenance Agent: system prompt + 5 `createTool` tools (zod inputs, re-validated with `checked()`), session state, `runRuleAgent(notice)` → streams `AgentEvent`s; the result comes from what was saved through the tools, never from the agent's text.\n- `src/server/ai.ts` also has `runToolAgent` (Cline SDK `Agent`, `openai-compatible` → Cline API): it is still the only module that talks to a model.\n- `src/server/adminApi.ts` + `src/app/api/admin/rules/**` (T3): propose (NDJSON stream), list (history + diff), `[id]/publish`, `[id]/reject`. `src/app/admin/` is the maintainer UI."}}}
